{"format":1,"number":11,"def":{"id":"case-11","title":"The Time Capsule","blurb":"The village's 1986 time capsule is to be opened at midnight on New Year's Eve. The night before, it vanishes from the harbour office.","scene":"harbour","chapters":[{"title":"The Empty Case","levels":[1,4],"intro":[{"who":"narrator","text":"New Year's Eve. In 1986 the village children buried a time capsule under the harbour wall. Tonight it will be opened."},{"who":"bryony","text":"We dug it up yesterday. I locked it in the display case in the harbour office at six, as the gate shut."},{"who":"narrator","text":"At seven this morning, the case was locked, and empty."},{"who":"goldie","text":"No scratches on the lock. Who has keys?"},{"who":"bryony","text":"My ring. And the committee spare, behind the bar at the Anchor. Anyone could reach that."},{"who":"biscuit","text":"Mrrp. (A key, then, not a crowbar. Let's find out who was busy last night.)"}],"clue":{"id":"opened-with-key","title":"Opened with a Key","text":"The display case was opened with a key and locked again. One key is on Bryony's ring; the committee spare hangs behind the bar at the Anchor, in reach of anyone.","allows":["bryony","ned","kit","silas"]}},{"title":"The Owl Count","levels":[5,8],"intro":[{"who":"kit","text":"I was up the church tower all night with the bird society. It's the winter owl count."},{"who":"kit","text":"Three of us, from six till seven in the morning. Every hour we wrote down the owls and all signed the page."},{"who":"goldie","text":"The owls in the clock tower? The ones you looked after?"},{"who":"biscuit","text":"Mrow. (Six owls, three counters and thirteen signed pages. Kit never came down.)"}],"clue":{"id":"owl-count","title":"The Owl Count","text":"Kit spent the night in the church tower with two others from the bird society, counting owls. Every page of the count, from six in the evening till seven in the morning, has all three signatures.","allows":["bryony","ned","silas"]}},{"title":"The Town Hall Clock","levels":[9,12],"intro":[{"who":"silas","text":"I was in Penmarrow. The town hall clock must strike midnight on the dot tonight. So they sent for Silas Penrose."},{"who":"silas","text":"Worked through the night with the caretaker. Signed in at six in the evening, out at six this morning."},{"who":"goldie","text":"And the first train doesn't get back here until after seven."},{"who":"biscuit","text":"Mrrp. (The caretaker's book doesn't lie. Unlike clocks that run fast.)"}],"clue":{"id":"caretakers-book","title":"The Caretaker's Book","text":"Silas spent the night mending the Penmarrow town hall clock. The caretaker's book has him signed in at six in the evening and out at six in the morning.","allows":["bryony","ned","kit"]}},{"title":"Two Hundred Pies","levels":[13,16],"intro":[{"who":"ned","text":"Two hundred Granny Pellow's Pies for the New Year party. Me and Mr Pellow baked all night."},{"who":"pellow","text":"Aye. Six in the evening till dawn. The ovens want turning every twenty minutes. Neither of us left that kitchen."},{"who":"goldie","text":"But the committee's spare key hangs right behind your bar, Ned."},{"who":"ned","text":"It does. And I never set foot behind the bar all night. Ask the pastry."},{"who":"biscuit","text":"Mrow. (Two hundred pies don't bake themselves. Ned was busy all night, with a witness.)"}],"clue":{"id":"two-hundred-pies","title":"Two Hundred Pies","text":"Ned and Mr Pellow baked pies in the Anchor's kitchen from six in the evening until dawn. The ovens needed turning every twenty minutes, and neither of them left.","allows":["bryony","kit","silas"]}},{"title":"The Gate Book","levels":[17,20],"intro":[{"who":"narrator","text":"Biscuit sits on the gate book in the harbour office. It is either a hint or a nap."},{"who":"goldie","text":"The harbour gate locks at six. After that you sign the book to be let in. Nobody signed it last night."},{"who":"bryony","text":"Then whoever came had their own gate key. There are two: mine, and Silas's, for winding the office clock."},{"who":"biscuit","text":"Mrrp. (Two gate keys. Now, where was each of them last night?)"}],"clue":{"id":"gate-book","title":"The Gate Book","text":"The harbour gate locks at six, and nobody signed the gate book that night, so the thief had a gate key. There are only two: Bryony's and Silas's.","allows":["bryony","silas"]}}],"suspects":[{"id":"bryony","label":"Bryony Trewin, the harbourmaster"},{"id":"ned","label":"Ned Polglase, the landlord"},{"id":"kit","label":"Kit Tremayne, the verger"},{"id":"silas","label":"Silas Penrose, the clockmaker"}],"culprit":"bryony","question":"Who took the time capsule?","accusePrompt":[{"who":"goldie","text":"Five clues, Biscuit. Who took the time capsule?"},{"who":"biscuit","text":"Mrrp. (Who wasn't counting owls, mending a clock or baking pies, and has a gate key?)"}],"wrongGuess":{"ned":[{"who":"biscuit","text":"Mrow. (Ned was turning pies in the Anchor's kitchen all night, with Mr Pellow beside him.)"}],"kit":[{"who":"biscuit","text":"Mrow. (Kit was up the church tower counting owls, and signed every page with two others.)"}],"silas":[{"who":"biscuit","text":"Mrow. (Silas was mending the town hall clock in Penmarrow until six. The caretaker's book says so.)"}]},"ending":[{"who":"goldie","text":"Bryony. Silas was in Penmarrow, so it was your gate key. And your key to the case."},{"who":"bryony","text":"Rules are rules. Yes. I took it. I put a letter in that capsule when I was ten."},{"who":"bryony","text":"'Dear grown-up Bryony. By now you've won the regatta and beaten every Pellow.' I never have. Not once."},{"who":"bryony","text":"I couldn't bear it read out at midnight, with the whole village there. With him there."},{"who":"goldie","text":"Is the capsule safe?"},{"who":"bryony","text":"On my kitchen table, seal unbroken. I couldn't bring myself to open it."},{"who":"narrator","text":"At midnight the capsule is opened, and Bryony's letter is read aloud. The harbour cheers louder than the fireworks."},{"who":"pellow","text":"Aye. Then sail the Gull with me this summer, Bryony Trewin. That way we both win it."},{"who":"biscuit","text":"Purrr. (Happy New Year. Now, about those two hundred pies.)"},{"who":"quill","text":"A new year, Goldie, and sad news. The council is lending the Kittiwake's figurehead to the museum in Penmarrow."}],"teaser":"Case 12: The Figurehead. Coming soon."},"levels":[{"seed":1100043,"board":{"filled":[0,0,99,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,99,0,0,0,0,0,0,99,99,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,99,0,0,0,0,99,99,0,99,0,0,0,0,0,99,0,99,0,99,0,0,0,99,99,0,0,0,99,0,0,99,99,0,0,99,99],"clues":[true,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,true,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false]},"pieces":[{"id":1,"cells":[[0,0],[0,1],[0,2],[0,3]],"colour":3},{"id":3,"cells":[[0,0],[1,0],[2,0],[3,0]],"colour":0},{"id":7,"cells":[[0,0],[0,1],[0,2]],"colour":4},{"id":6,"cells":[[0,0],[0,1]],"colour":1},{"id":4,"cells":[[0,0]],"colour":4},{"id":5,"cells":[[0,0],[1,0]],"colour":0},{"id":2,"cells":[[0,0],[0,1],[0,2]],"colour":5},{"id":10,"cells":[[0,0],[1,0]],"colour":0},{"id":11,"cells":[[0,0],[0,1]],"colour":4},{"id":8,"cells":[[0,0],[0,1]],"colour":4},{"id":9,"cells":[[0,0]],"colour":4}],"solution":[{"pieceId":1,"row":1,"col":4},{"pieceId":3,"row":2,"col":0},{"pieceId":4,"row":0,"col":0},{"pieceId":5,"row":6,"col":0},{"pieceId":2,"row":1,"col":0}],"winRate":0.76875},{"seed":1100062,"board":{"filled":[0,99,99,0,0,99,0,99,0,99,0,0,99,99,99,0,0,0,99,99,0,0,0,0,0,99,0,0,0,99,99,99,0,0,0,0,0,99,0,99,99,0,0,99,0,0,0,99,99,0,0,0,99,0,99,0,0,99,0,0,0,0,0,0],"clues":[false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,true,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,fa